<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Authari</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 590</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Authari was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombards</a> from 584 to 590, chosen after a ten-year interregnum during which the dukes had ruled without a king. He restored royal power, defended Lombard <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> against Frankish and Byzantine attacks and in 589 married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodelinda">Theodelinda</a>, daughter of the Bavarian duke Garibald I. He died in 590, probably poisoned, and Theodelinda's choice of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agilulf">Agilulf</a> as her next husband made him king.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/authari.jpg" alt="Authari" width="251" height="302" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michel Wolgemut, Wilhelm Pleydenwurff (Text: Hartmann Schedel) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nuremberg_chronicles_f_150r_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
